UPDATE lessons SET
  content = '[
    {"type":"video","youtube_id":"7dfPQjGJ0es"},
    {"type":"text","body":"Your first check is fuel, not a finish line. The most common mistake beginners make is closing their first deal, celebrating, spending most of the check on lifestyle, and then wondering why the next month is empty. One deal becomes a paycheck back to zero if you stop feeding the top of the funnel.\n\nThe rule is simple. Before you pay yourself heavy, fund your next month of lead generation. Sixty to eighty percent of your first check should go back into leads: more SMS, more list pulls, more marketing spend. Ten to twenty-five percent should go into basic systems that stop chaos: a simple CRM like GoHighLevel, a dialer, or a VA for ten to twenty hours a week. Five to fifteen percent can be a small win reward if you want one, but only after everything else is funded.\n\nUpgrade your marketing when you can prove you close deals from your current source, when you can afford sixty days of spend without panicking, and when the results are consistent instead of spiky. Start with basic outreach and SMS. Add a VA once volume gets chaotic. Layer in Facebook or Google ads once your process is solid and your dispo is fast. Cheaper lead generation is less predictable. Better lead generation is more predictable. Not more expensive. Better."},
    {"type":"quiz","id":"q1","question":"What should the majority of your first check go toward?","options":["A win reward for yourself","More lead generation for the next month","Paying off personal debt","Software subscriptions"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Sixty to eighty percent back into leads. Thats how you stop being a paycheck-to-zero business."},
    {"type":"quiz","id":"q2","question":"Whats the biggest mistake beginners make after their first deal?","options":["Reinvesting too much money","Stopping the marketing that created the deal","Signing another contract too fast","Hiring too many virtual assistants"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Deals fall through, buyers flake. Lead flow is what makes your business survivable."},
    {"type":"quiz","id":"q3","question":"When should you upgrade to better marketing like Google ads?","options":["When your current system is proven and you can afford 60 days of spend","Right after closing your first deal","Before you close any deals","Only after 5 years in the business"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Predictable lead gen isnt better because its more expensive. Its better because your systems are ready for it."},
    {"type":"quiz","id":"q4","question":"Whats the danger of hiring a closer before you have lead volume?","options":["They will steal your buyers","A closer cant close leads that dont exist","They will charge too much","They will report you to the IRS"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Dont hire people ahead of your lead volume. Fix the top of the funnel first."},
    {"type":"quiz","id":"q5","question":"What is the cycle that keeps a wholesaling business alive?","options":["Leads to conversations to contracts to closings to more leads","Marketing to cashflow to vacation to repeat","Buy to hold to rent to sell","Cold call to close to celebrate to stop"],"correct":0,"explanation":"If closings dont fund more leads, youre back to zero next month."}
  ]'::jsonb,
  updated_at = now()
WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM courses WHERE slug = 'scaling') AND sort_order = 1;

UPDATE lessons SET
  content = '[
    {"type":"video","youtube_id":"UsGpg5tI4ZE"},
    {"type":"text","body":"Three real deals from real students, all closed in their first three months. These are the pattern.\n\nDylan found a deal in St. Louis through an agent connection. Locked up at 78K, comps put it at 150K. Got paid 5K on assignment. Two more deals under contract with the same buyer at the time of recording. Roughly 10K in his first 60 days.\n\nMelissa found a property in Scott City, Missouri sitting on Zillow. Had the seller unlist and sell directly. Locked up at 39K after negotiating down from 50K. Comps around 100K. Got paid 4K on assignment. Another deal almost under contract now.\n\nEve found a deal in Granite City, Illinois on Zillow. Made an offer to the listing agent on state forms. Locked up at 60K, comps at 115K. The roof came back bad in inspection so the seller installed a new roof before closing. Got paid 5K, then another 3K on his second deal. Eight thousand cushion in his first three months while working a 60-hour week at his day job. Now scaling with VAs.\n\nWhat is repeatable here is not any specific tactic. It is the pattern. Take action, source deals that match a real buyer, use the profits to buy more opportunities, stack the reps. That is the entire game."},
    {"type":"quiz","id":"q1","question":"What is the common pattern across all three case studies?","options":["They all used the same lead source","They all closed their first deals within three months by taking consistent action","They all had prior real estate experience","They all had large starting budgets"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Different sources, different states. Same pattern: consistent action, fast reps."},
    {"type":"quiz","id":"q2","question":"How did Dylan find his first deal in St. Louis?","options":["Through an agent connection who was teaming up with another wholesaler","By sending SMS blasts","By running Google ads","By cold-calling absentee owners"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Dylans deal came through his agent connection. Assignment of contract, 5K to Dylan."},
    {"type":"quiz","id":"q3","question":"How did Melissa find her first deal in Scott City, Missouri?","options":["Through a Facebook group","Sitting on Zillow. She had the seller unlist it and sell directly","By door-knocking","Through a wholesaler friend"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Melissa found it on Zillow, got it unlisted, and closed direct-to-seller for a 4K assignment."},
    {"type":"quiz","id":"q4","question":"In Eves Granite City deal, what happened during inspection?","options":["The buyer backed out","The roof was bad, but the seller installed a new one before closing","The title company canceled the deal","The seller raised the price"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Seller installed a fresh roof before close. Eve got paid 5K, then 3K on his next deal."},
    {"type":"quiz","id":"q5","question":"What did all three students do with their profits?","options":["Quit their day jobs immediately","Used them to scale their businesses with VAs and more marketing","Spent them on lifestyle upgrades","Bought their first rental properties"],"correct":1,"explanation":"They kept the profits as fuel. Thats the difference between one deal and a real business."}
  ]'::jsonb,
  updated_at = now()
WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM courses WHERE slug = 'scaling') AND sort_order = 2;
